course: dictionary
lesson: 1820
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. A dictionary gives each meaning a number, but when you read, the sentence tells you which meaning is right. Clutch is a good example: it can mean holding something tightly, or a group of eggs.
explain: Look at «A modern laying hen can lay about 300 eggs a year, nearly one a day, while her wild ancestor lays only a few clutches of five or six.» Hens and eggs are the clues, so clutches means groups of eggs laid at one time. Clutch can also be a verb: a child clutches a teddy when she is scared.
explain: Ask yourself what the topic is and which words are nearby. Then put your meaning into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right one.
fact: Clutch can be a verb, a noun, or an adjective in US slang.
fact: «To clutch» means to hold something tightly, often because you are afraid, in pain, or don't want to lose it.
fact: A clutch of eggs is a group of eggs laid at one time by a bird.
fact: In a car, the clutch is a pedal you press to change gear.
fact: «Clutch at straws» means trying anything when there is little hope.
exercise: «She clutched her ticket tightly all the way to the stadium.» What does clutched mean? | Read it aloud | Threw it away | *Held tightly, not wanting to lose it | Tore it into pieces
exercise: «The hen sat on her clutch of eggs.» What is a clutch here? | *A group of eggs laid at one time | A pair of gloves | A pedal in a car | A small handbag
exercise: «Dad pressed the clutch to change gear.» Which meaning fits this sentence? | A group of eggs | *A pedal in a car used to change gears | Trying to grab something quickly | In someone's power or control
test: «The climber clutched at the rope as she slipped.» What does clutched at mean? | Waved happily | Painted over | Let go slowly | *Grabbed quickly, trying to hold on
test: «The mouse was in the clutches of the cat.» What does clutches mean here? | Sharp, pointed teeth | *In the power or control of someone | Hands with long nails | A small handbag
exam: «In the final minute, she made a clutch shot to win the match.» What does clutch mean here? | A pedal in a car | A group of eggs | To hold something tightly | *Very good at doing well in a tense, important moment
